1
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:25,030
You could've killed me.

2
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:35,120
The fuck were you doing back there?

3
00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:36,890
Ending the war.

4
00:02:37,450 --> 00:02:38,470
Killing her.

5
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:42,330
You saw the dragon between you and her?

6
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:46,170
And?

7
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:56,250
Listen to me, cunt.

8
00:02:56,730 --> 00:02:58,220
Till I get what I'm owed,

9
00:02:58,250 --> 00:03:00,050
a dragon doesn't get to kill you,

10
00:03:00,130 --> 00:03:01,710
you don't get to kill you,

11
00:03:02,090 --> 00:03:03,880
only I get to kill you.

12
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:08,680
That was only one of them.

13
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,120
She has two more.

14
00:03:12,730 --> 00:03:15,650
If she decides to use them, to really use them...

15
00:03:15,650 --> 00:03:17,980
- You're fucked. - Don't you mean we're fucked?

16
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:19,200
No, I do not.

17
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:22,350
Dragons are where our partnership ends.

18
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:24,850
I'm not gonna be around when those things

19
00:03:24,850 --> 00:03:26,870
start spitting fire on King's Landing.

20
00:03:28,590 --> 00:03:30,080
I have to tell Cersei.

21
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,780
May as well jump back in that river.

22
00:04:49,570 --> 00:04:51,630
I know what Cersei has told you.

23
00:04:53,010 --> 00:04:56,010
That I've come to destroy your cities,

24
00:04:56,770 --> 00:04:58,140
burn down your homes,

25
00:04:58,140 --> 00:05:00,250
murder you, and orphan your children.

26
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:05,590
That's Cersei Lannister, not me.

27
00:05:06,690 --> 00:05:08,390
I'm not here to murder,

28
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:10,640
and all I want to destroy

29
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:13,800
is the wheel that has rolled over rich and poor

30
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:17,450
to the benefit of no one but the Cersei Lannisters of the world.

31
00:05:19,130 --> 00:05:20,880
I offer you a choice--

32
00:05:21,630 --> 00:05:23,520
bend the knee and join me.

33
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:25,570
Together, we will leave

34
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:28,010
the world a better place than we found it.

35
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:29,640
Or refuse...

36
00:05:30,890 --> 00:05:31,920
and die.

37
00:06:01,290 --> 00:06:02,660
Step forward, my lord.

38
00:06:12,450 --> 00:06:13,590
You will not kneel?

39
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:15,430
I already have a queen.

40
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:17,790
My sister.

41
00:06:18,390 --> 00:06:20,910
She wasn't your queen until recently, though, was she?

42
00:06:21,390 --> 00:06:23,520
When she murdered your rightful queen

43
00:06:23,660 --> 00:06:26,100
and destroyed House Tyrell for all time.

44
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:29,850
So it appears your allegiances are somewhat flexible.

45
00:06:30,740 --> 00:06:32,880
There are no easy choices in war.

46
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:35,640
Say what you will about your sister,

47
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:37,630
she was born in Westeros.

48
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:40,460
She's lived here all her life.

49
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:44,350
You, on the other hand,

50
00:06:45,690 --> 00:06:47,530
murdered your own father

51
00:06:48,450 --> 00:06:51,270
and chose to support a foreign invader.

52
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:53,840
One with no ties to this land...

53
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,380
with an army of savages at her back.

54
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:02,240
You will not trade your honor for your life.

55
00:07:03,710 --> 00:07:04,960
I respect that.

56
00:07:06,030 --> 00:07:08,330
Perhaps he could take the Black, Your Grace.

57
00:07:08,610 --> 00:07:10,960
Whatever else he is, he is a true soldier.

58
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:12,860
He'd be invaluable at the Wall.

59
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,910
You cannot send me to the Wall.

60
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:18,620
You are not my queen.

61
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,500
You will have to kill me, too.

62
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:35,500
Step back and shut your mouth.

63
00:07:36,750 --> 00:07:37,640
Who are you?

64
00:07:38,170 --> 00:07:39,390
A stupid boy.

65
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:41,760
I am Dickon Tarly,

66
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:44,150
son of Randyll Tarly.

67
00:07:44,270 --> 00:07:46,440
You are the future of your house.

68
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:49,560
This war has already wiped one great house from the world.

69
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:51,790
Don't let it happen again. Bend the knee.

70
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,110
I will not.

71
00:08:05,150 --> 00:08:08,650
Your Grace, nothing scrubs bold notions from a man's head

72
00:08:08,650 --> 00:08:10,390
like a few weeks in a dark cell.

73
00:08:10,390 --> 00:08:11,970
I meant what I said.

74
00:08:12,730 --> 00:08:14,520
I'm not here to put men in chains.

75
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:16,840
If that becomes an option, many will take it.

76
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,280
I gave them a choice.

77
00:08:19,990 --> 00:08:21,240
They made it.

78
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:24,220
Your Grace, if you start beheading entire families--

79
00:08:24,230 --> 00:08:25,780
I'm not beheading anyone.

80
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:33,440
Your Grace.

81
00:08:57,740 --> 00:09:00,430
Lord Randyll Tarly, Dickon Tarly,

82
00:09:00,870 --> 00:09:04,220
I, Daenerys of House Targaryen, First of My Name,

83
00:09:04,230 --> 00:09:06,930
Breaker of Chains, and Mother of Dragons,

84
00:09:06,930 --> 00:09:08,610
sentence you to die.

85
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:13,810
Dracarys.

86
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:02,630
My-- my lord...

87
00:10:13,010 --> 00:10:14,860
How many men did we lose?

88
00:10:17,150 --> 00:10:18,890
We haven't done a full accounting.

89
00:10:21,010 --> 00:10:23,160
It's not only armies that win wars.

90
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:26,650
We have the Tyrell gold, we have the Iron Bank behind us.

91
00:10:26,650 --> 00:10:28,370
We can buy mercenaries.

92
00:10:30,590 --> 00:10:32,340
Not the same as our men, but they'll fight

93
00:10:32,350 --> 00:10:34,490
if they're well paid, which they will be.

94
00:10:34,490 --> 00:10:36,910
I just saw the Dothraki fight.

95
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,710
They'll beat any mercenary army.

96
00:10:39,710 --> 00:10:41,670
They'll beat any army I've ever seen.

97
00:10:41,670 --> 00:10:44,380
Killing our men wasn't war for them, it was sport.

98
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:46,730
Her dragon burnt a thousand wagons.

99
00:10:46,730 --> 00:10:48,910
Qyburn's scorpion fired bolts bigger than you.

100
00:10:48,910 --> 00:10:51,310
They couldn't stop it. And she has three of them.

101
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:55,420
This isn't a war we can win.

102
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:56,590
So, what do we do?

103
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,490
Sue for peace?

104
00:11:00,710 --> 00:11:02,390
I sit on her father's throne,

105
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:04,590
the father you betrayed and murdered.

106
00:11:05,090 --> 00:11:07,040
And in her mind, she's winning.

107
00:11:08,050 --> 00:11:10,020
What sort of offer do you think she'd make?

108
00:11:12,450 --> 00:11:15,580
Maybe we can count on Tyrion to intercede on our behalf

109
00:11:15,670 --> 00:11:18,660
by way of apology for murdering our father and son.

110
00:11:20,150 --> 00:11:21,170
He didn't.

111
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:23,180
You saw the crossbow, you saw his body.

112
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:25,040
I'm not talking about Father.

113
00:11:25,470 --> 00:11:28,250
Tyrion didn't kill Joffrey. He had nothing to do with it.

114
00:11:29,290 --> 00:11:30,260
After all this time,

115
00:11:30,260 --> 00:11:32,410
- it still amazes me that you-- - It was Olenna.

116
00:11:34,590 --> 00:11:36,500
She confessed before she died.

117
00:11:39,110 --> 00:11:41,470
And this was before or after

118
00:11:41,470 --> 00:11:44,430
she drank the poison you so kindly provided her?

119
00:11:44,890 --> 00:11:45,870
After.

120
00:11:45,870 --> 00:11:47,150
And you believed her?

121
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:50,370
If you were Olenna, would you rather have seen

122
00:11:50,370 --> 00:11:53,300
your granddaughter married to Joffrey or Tommen?

123
00:11:55,610 --> 00:11:57,750
Which one would Margaery have been better able to control?

124
00:11:57,750 --> 00:12:01,930
Which one would have made Olenna the true ruler of the Seven Kingdoms?

125
00:12:02,110 --> 00:12:03,690
She was telling the truth.

126
00:12:11,510 --> 00:12:13,220
I shouldn't have listened to you.

127
00:12:15,490 --> 00:12:17,210
She should have died screaming.

128
00:12:17,210 --> 00:12:18,560
She's dead, like her son,

129
00:12:18,570 --> 00:12:20,480
her grandchildren, her whole house.

130
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:22,530
And if we don't find a way out of this war,

131
00:12:22,530 --> 00:12:24,140
we'll follow them.

132
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:26,400
So we fight and die or we submit and die.

133
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:27,980
I know my choice.

134
00:12:28,870 --> 00:12:30,610
A soldier should know his.

135
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:39,770
They're beautiful, aren't they?

136
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:43,030
It wasn't the word I was thinking of, but...

137
00:14:44,650 --> 00:14:46,630
but, yes, they are.

138
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:49,010
Gorgeous beasts.

139
00:14:49,010 --> 00:14:50,620
They're not beasts to me.

140
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:52,590
No matter how big they get

141
00:14:52,590 --> 00:14:54,650
or how terrifying to everyone else,

142
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:56,470
they're my children.

143
00:15:02,190 --> 00:15:03,440
You weren't gone long.

144
00:15:04,190 --> 00:15:04,940
No.

145
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:06,540
And?

146
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:10,510
And I have fewer enemies today than I did yesterday.

147
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,210
You're not sure how you feel about that.

148
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:17,220
No, I'm not.

149
00:15:18,790 --> 00:15:22,510
How many men did your army kill taking Winterfell back from the Boltons?

150
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:24,420
Thousands.

151
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:26,430
We both want to help people.

152
00:15:26,990 --> 00:15:29,750
We can only help them from a position of strength.

153
00:15:30,690 --> 00:15:32,400
Sometimes strength is terrible.

154
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:37,300
When you first came here,

155
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:41,670
Ser Davos said you took a knife in the heart for your people.

156
00:15:42,430 --> 00:15:44,150
Ser Davos gets carried away.

157
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:47,400
So, it was a figure of speech?

158
00:16:08,110 --> 00:16:09,190
Your Grace.

159
00:16:15,030 --> 00:16:17,470
Jon Snow, this is Ser Jorah Mormont,

160
00:16:18,470 --> 00:16:19,640
an old friend.

161
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:21,890
I served with your father.

162
00:16:22,910 --> 00:16:24,150
He was a great man.

163
00:16:25,830 --> 00:16:27,070
You look strong.

164
00:16:29,370 --> 00:16:30,520
You found a cure?

165
00:16:30,790 --> 00:16:32,440
I wouldn't be here if I hadn't.

166
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:35,680
I return to your service, my queen,

167
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:38,460
if you'll have me.

168
00:16:39,490 --> 00:16:40,930
It would be my honor.

169
00:18:20,510 --> 00:18:21,490
Ravens.

170
00:18:22,150 --> 00:18:23,610
We need to send ravens.

171
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:29,310
I put very little stock in it myself.

172
00:18:29,410 --> 00:18:31,600
Prophecies of doom are never in short supply,

173
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:33,170
especially when winter comes.

174
00:18:33,770 --> 00:18:35,470
I remember Wolkan.

175
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:38,430
A little timid, but a sharp mind.

176
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:41,640
Eh, the North has dulled many good maesters' wits.

177
00:18:41,990 --> 00:18:44,160
Hard to say whether it's the cold, the drink,

178
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:45,580
or the company.

179
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:48,040
A crippled boy claims to have seen

180
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:50,030
dead men on the march beyond the Wall,

181
00:18:50,030 --> 00:18:53,810
thanks to the magical help of a raven with three eyes?

182
00:18:53,810 --> 00:18:55,370
Yes, it is a bit much.

183
00:18:55,470 --> 00:18:57,750
- Still, we ought to write back-- - Brandon Stark.

184
00:19:01,350 --> 00:19:04,950
- The crippled boy. - Do you know him?

185
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:07,660
I led him through the Wall years ago.

186
00:19:07,850 --> 00:19:09,930
I saw him go beyond the Wall.

187
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:12,950
And?

188
00:19:13,310 --> 00:19:15,450
Somehow, a crippled boy

189
00:19:15,450 --> 00:19:18,230
survived for years beyond the Wall when no one else could.

190
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:21,720
Not the Night's Watch, not the wildlings, no one.

191
00:19:22,980 --> 00:19:25,030
Perhaps we ought to listen to what he has to say.

192
00:19:25,190 --> 00:19:28,320
Perhaps you need more scribing work to discipline your mind.

193
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:32,110
I sense a more detailed proposal is forthcoming?

194
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:45,090
Everyone in Westeros trusts and respects you.

195
00:19:46,570 --> 00:19:49,590
If you tell people the threat is real, they'll believe it.

196
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:52,560
If you advise all the lords to send their men north

197
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:54,650
to hold the Wall, they'll do it.

198
00:19:55,780 --> 00:19:58,150
And if you tell every maester in the Citadel

199
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:00,280
to search every word of every faded scroll

200
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:02,000
about the Long Night,

201
00:20:02,420 --> 00:20:03,960
they may find something that lets us defeat

202
00:20:03,960 --> 00:20:05,810
the Army of the Dead for good.

203
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,660
It could be done.

204
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:16,350
And this news could be authentic.

205
00:20:16,570 --> 00:20:17,820
It's possible.

206
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:22,810
It's also possible that this message

207
00:20:22,810 --> 00:20:25,210
is part of a ploy by the Dragon Queen

208
00:20:25,510 --> 00:20:26,550
to lure southern armies away

209
00:20:26,550 --> 00:20:28,120
from the lands they are currently defending

210
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:30,470
to open those lands to easy conquest.

211
00:20:30,470 --> 00:20:31,600
That does seem far more likely

212
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:34,020
than magic birds talking to cripples.

213
00:20:34,020 --> 00:20:35,670
Archmaester, please.

214
00:20:36,350 --> 00:20:37,440
It's real.

215
00:20:39,590 --> 00:20:40,890
I've seen it.

216
00:20:43,630 --> 00:20:44,930
We will write to Maester Wolkan

217
00:20:44,930 --> 00:20:46,980
at Winterfell for clarification.

218
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:50,300
I promise you we will get to the truth of it one way or another.

219
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:52,910
- Archmaester, please-- - That will be all, Tarly.

220
00:20:53,240 --> 00:20:55,540
It brings to mind the work of Jenny of Oldstones,

221
00:20:55,540 --> 00:20:56,620
the charlatan who claimed

222
00:20:56,620 --> 00:20:59,140
descent from the children of the forest.

223
00:20:59,310 --> 00:21:00,450
Don't forget the prophet Lodos,

224
00:21:00,450 --> 00:21:01,590
who promised that the Drowned

225
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:04,680
God would rise up and destroy Aegon the Conqueror.

226
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:06,330
Ah, Lodos.

227
00:21:10,420 --> 00:21:14,210
Is he the one whose father and brother were just burnt alive?

228
00:21:14,790 --> 00:21:16,090
I'm afraid so.

229
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:17,980
Horrible business.

230
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:20,230
I haven't had the heart to tell him yet.

231
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:22,150
He's a good lad.

232
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:24,270
Right.

233
00:21:24,450 --> 00:21:27,650
The ravenry was falling apart the last time I checked.

234
00:21:32,680 --> 00:21:35,190
All rulers demand that people bend the knee.

235
00:21:35,190 --> 00:21:36,750
That's why they're rulers.

236
00:21:39,470 --> 00:21:41,350
She gave Tarly a choice,

237
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:43,700
a man who had taken up arms against her.

238
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:46,010
What else could she do?

239
00:21:46,380 --> 00:21:49,240
Not burn him alive alongside his son?

240
00:21:49,260 --> 00:21:51,520
I am her Hand, not her head.

241
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:53,850
I can't make her decisions for her.

242
00:21:53,870 --> 00:21:56,660
That's what I used to tell myself about her father.

243
00:21:57,350 --> 00:22:01,090
I found the traitors, but I wasn't the one burning them alive.

244
00:22:01,660 --> 00:22:04,410
I was only a purveyor of information.

245
00:22:09,410 --> 00:22:13,110
It's what I told myself when I watched them beg for mercy--

246
00:22:13,330 --> 00:22:15,390
I'm not the one doing it.

247
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:18,250
When the pitch of their screams rose higher--

248
00:22:18,260 --> 00:22:20,580
I'm not the one doing it.

249
00:22:20,580 --> 00:22:21,970
When their hair caught fire

250
00:22:21,970 --> 00:22:24,350
and the smell of their burning flesh filled the throne room--

251
00:22:24,350 --> 00:22:26,970
I'm not the one doing it.

252
00:22:35,340 --> 00:22:37,460
Daenerys is not her father.

253
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:38,990
And she never will be

254
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:41,760
with the right counsel.

255
00:22:45,290 --> 00:22:48,010
You need to find a way to make her listen.

256
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:52,990
- Who's that for? - Jon Snow.

257
00:22:53,510 --> 00:22:55,060
Did you read it?

258
00:22:55,090 --> 00:22:58,310
It's a sealed scroll for the King in the North.

259
00:23:04,340 --> 00:23:05,630
What's it say?

260
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:07,930
Nothing good.

261
00:23:14,610 --> 00:23:16,570
I thought Arya was dead.

262
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:20,390
I thought Bran was dead.

263
00:23:21,490 --> 00:23:22,820
I'm happy for you.

264
00:23:25,160 --> 00:23:26,630
You don't look happy.

265
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:28,540
Bran saw the Night King and his army

266
00:23:28,540 --> 00:23:30,700
marching towards Eastwatch.

267
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:33,960
If they make it past the Wall...

268
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:36,750
The Wall has kept them out for thousands of years, presumably.

269
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:38,240
I need to go home.

270
00:23:38,590 --> 00:23:40,320
You said you don't have enough men.

271
00:23:40,330 --> 00:23:42,260
We'll fight with the men we have.

272
00:23:43,100 --> 00:23:44,540
Unless you'll join us.

273
00:23:44,540 --> 00:23:46,620
And give the country to Cersei?

274
00:23:46,860 --> 00:23:49,300
As soon as I march away, she marches in.

275
00:23:50,600 --> 00:23:51,900
Perhaps not.

276
00:23:53,690 --> 00:23:56,320
Cersei thinks the Army of the Dead is nothing but a story

277
00:23:56,460 --> 00:23:59,040
made up by wet nurses to frighten children.

278
00:24:00,050 --> 00:24:01,650
What if we prove her wrong?

279
00:24:02,220 --> 00:24:05,360
I don't think she'll come see the dead at my invitation.

280
00:24:06,190 --> 00:24:08,390
So bring the dead to her.

281
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:11,780
I thought that was what we were trying to avoid.

282
00:24:11,860 --> 00:24:13,600
We don't have to bring the whole army.

283
00:24:13,850 --> 00:24:15,430
Only one soldier.

284
00:24:16,100 --> 00:24:17,570
Is that possible?

285
00:24:22,010 --> 00:24:23,100
The first wight I ever saw

286
00:24:23,100 --> 00:24:25,560
was brought into Castle Black from beyond the Wall.

287
00:24:26,630 --> 00:24:28,590
Bring one of these things down to King's Landing

288
00:24:28,590 --> 00:24:30,430
and show her the truth.

289
00:24:30,810 --> 00:24:32,720
Anything you bring back will be useless

290
00:24:32,720 --> 00:24:34,360
unless Cersei grants us an audience

291
00:24:34,360 --> 00:24:36,950
and is somehow convinced not to murder us

292
00:24:36,950 --> 00:24:39,520
the moment we set foot in the capital.

293
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:42,070
The only person she listens to is Jaime.

294
00:24:43,230 --> 00:24:44,820
He might listen to me.

295
00:24:48,870 --> 00:24:51,080
And how would you get into King's Landing?

296
00:24:56,770 --> 00:24:58,430
I can smuggle you in,

297
00:24:58,970 --> 00:25:01,350
but if the gold cloaks were to recognize you,

298
00:25:01,350 --> 00:25:03,450
I'm warning you, I'm not a fighter.

299
00:25:04,590 --> 00:25:05,640
Well, it will all be for nothing

300
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:07,730
if we don't have one of these dead men.

301
00:25:07,740 --> 00:25:09,030
Fair point.

302
00:25:09,030 --> 00:25:11,050
How do you propose to find one?

303
00:25:14,080 --> 00:25:17,070
With the queen's permission, I'll go north and take one.

304
00:25:18,990 --> 00:25:21,880
You asked me to find a cure so I could serve you.

305
00:25:22,310 --> 00:25:23,900
Allow me to serve you.

306
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:29,590
The Free Folk will help us.

307
00:25:30,030 --> 00:25:31,840
They know the real north better than anyone.

308
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:33,630
They won't follow Ser Jorah.

309
00:25:33,670 --> 00:25:35,100
They won't have to.

310
00:25:41,750 --> 00:25:43,820
You can't lead a raid beyond the Wall.

311
00:25:44,300 --> 00:25:45,790
You're not in the Night's Watch anymore,

312
00:25:45,790 --> 00:25:46,750
you're King in the North.

313
00:25:46,750 --> 00:25:49,050
I'm the only one here who's fought them.

314
00:25:49,480 --> 00:25:51,780
I'm the only one here who knows them.

315
00:25:53,240 --> 00:25:55,060
I haven't given you permission to leave.

316
00:25:57,900 --> 00:26:00,670
With respect, Your Grace, I don't need your permission.

317
00:26:01,470 --> 00:26:02,700
I am a king.

318
00:26:04,170 --> 00:26:05,530
And I came here

319
00:26:05,530 --> 00:26:07,200
knowing that you could have your men behead me

320
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:09,530
or your dragons burn me alive.

321
00:26:10,750 --> 00:26:14,850
I put my trust in you, a stranger,

322
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:17,840
because I knew it was the best chance for my people,

323
00:26:17,850 --> 00:26:20,100
for all our people.

324
00:26:21,810 --> 00:26:26,250
Now I'm asking you to trust in a stranger...

325
00:26:27,970 --> 00:26:29,980
because it's our best chance.

326
00:26:48,630 --> 00:26:52,720
The King in the North should stay in the North.

327
00:26:55,360 --> 00:26:58,950
We did not choose you to rule us, my lady.

328
00:26:59,860 --> 00:27:02,020
But perhaps we should have.

329
00:27:04,910 --> 00:27:09,610
The Knights of the Vale came here for you, Lady Stark.

330
00:27:15,680 --> 00:27:18,160
You are very kind, my lords.

331
00:27:19,040 --> 00:27:20,960
But Jon is our king.

332
00:27:21,130 --> 00:27:23,410
He is doing what he thinks is best.

333
00:27:33,540 --> 00:27:35,580
I warned Jon this would happen.

334
00:27:35,990 --> 00:27:37,240
That he couldn't leave the North

335
00:27:37,240 --> 00:27:39,940
and expect it to just sit and wait for him like Ghost.

336
00:27:39,940 --> 00:27:42,650
He didn't. He trusted you to hold it for him.

337
00:27:42,650 --> 00:27:45,540
Well, he's not making it easy. The Northern lords are proud.

338
00:27:50,230 --> 00:27:52,310
These are Mother and Father's chambers.

339
00:27:52,950 --> 00:27:54,060
And?

340
00:27:56,680 --> 00:27:57,900
Nothing.

341
00:27:58,710 --> 00:28:00,100
Don't do that.

342
00:28:01,420 --> 00:28:03,680
- What? - Say what you mean.

343
00:28:05,710 --> 00:28:08,220
You always liked nice things.

344
00:28:09,570 --> 00:28:11,650
They made you feel better than everyone.

345
00:28:16,760 --> 00:28:18,300
Are you angry with me?

346
00:28:18,300 --> 00:28:20,270
They were insulting Jon,

347
00:28:20,940 --> 00:28:22,090
and you sat there and listened.

348
00:28:22,090 --> 00:28:23,560
I listened to their complaints,

349
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:26,710
which is my responsibility as Lady of Winterfell.

350
00:28:26,710 --> 00:28:28,830
Their opinions are important to you.

351
00:28:29,620 --> 00:28:32,050
Glover has 500 men, Royce has 2,000.

352
00:28:32,050 --> 00:28:35,290
Offend them and Jon loses his army.

353
00:28:35,300 --> 00:28:37,430
Not if they lose their heads first.

354
00:28:40,800 --> 00:28:44,060
Winterfell didn't just fall into our hands.

355
00:28:44,060 --> 00:28:45,640
We took it back,

356
00:28:45,690 --> 00:28:47,580
and the Mormonts and the Hornwoods

357
00:28:47,580 --> 00:28:49,170
and the wildlings and the Vale.

358
00:28:49,170 --> 00:28:50,660
All of us, working together.

359
00:28:50,660 --> 00:28:55,090
Now, I'm sure cutting off heads is very satisfying,

360
00:28:55,090 --> 00:28:58,680
but that's not the way you get people to work together.

361
00:29:01,700 --> 00:29:03,850
And if Jon doesn't come back,

362
00:29:04,100 --> 00:29:05,860
you'll need their support...

363
00:29:06,110 --> 00:29:07,790
so you can work together

364
00:29:08,180 --> 00:29:10,040
to give you what you really want.

365
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:13,060
How can you even think such a horrible thing?

366
00:29:15,450 --> 00:29:17,300
You're thinking it right now.

367
00:29:19,690 --> 00:29:21,410
You don't want to be,

368
00:29:22,490 --> 00:29:24,720
but the thought just won't go away.

369
00:29:30,560 --> 00:29:32,460
I have work to do.

370
00:29:36,150 --> 00:29:37,410
My lady.

371
00:29:49,440 --> 00:29:53,010
Last time I was here, I killed my father with a crossbow.

372
00:29:53,030 --> 00:29:56,060
Last time I was here, you killed my son with wildfire.

373
00:29:58,950 --> 00:30:01,630
There's a path to the left that hugs the cliff.

374
00:30:01,870 --> 00:30:04,060
The guards hardly ever patrol it.

375
00:30:04,450 --> 00:30:05,790
Too many steps.

376
00:30:10,820 --> 00:30:12,090
You're not staying here?

377
00:30:12,090 --> 00:30:14,100
I've got my own business in Flea Bottom.

378
00:30:15,640 --> 00:30:17,080
What if someone takes the boat?

379
00:30:17,080 --> 00:30:19,800
Then we're fucked. Best hurry.

380
00:30:25,660 --> 00:30:26,590
We don't have time for this.

381
00:30:26,590 --> 00:30:28,340
We should be preparing the city for a siege.

382
00:30:28,340 --> 00:30:29,500
The Dothraki are coming.

383
00:30:29,500 --> 00:30:31,430
All the more reason for you to train.

384
00:30:31,430 --> 00:30:33,530
Unless you plan on fighting Dothraki 12-year-olds.

385
00:30:33,530 --> 00:30:36,180
Well, I seem to recall them giving you a bit of trouble as well.

386
00:30:36,180 --> 00:30:38,120
And here I am, ready to train.

387
00:30:38,120 --> 00:30:39,570
Why down here?

388
00:30:40,380 --> 00:30:42,010
I don't think you want people to see

389
00:30:42,010 --> 00:30:44,420
how you look swinging that thing yet.

390
00:30:45,270 --> 00:30:47,820
Today might be the day I kill you by accident.

391
00:30:47,820 --> 00:30:50,880
Oh, you won't be swinging it at me.

392
00:30:58,420 --> 00:31:00,730
I'll leave you to it.

393
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:05,500
I needed to see you.

394
00:31:06,730 --> 00:31:09,050
And I knew you'd never agree to meet.

395
00:31:12,230 --> 00:31:14,470
You made me look like a complete fool.

396
00:31:15,380 --> 00:31:18,040
I thought I'd surprise you by hitting Casterly Rock,

397
00:31:18,490 --> 00:31:20,270
but you were three steps ahead of me.

398
00:31:20,530 --> 00:31:23,420
Abandoned the family home, completely unsentimental.

399
00:31:23,470 --> 00:31:24,540
Father would have been proud.

400
00:31:24,540 --> 00:31:25,940
- Don't talk about Father. - Listen to me--

401
00:31:25,940 --> 00:31:27,650
I once told Bronn

402
00:31:28,220 --> 00:31:31,090
that if I ever saw you again, I'd cut you in half.

403
00:31:33,650 --> 00:31:36,250
It'll take you a while with a sparring sword.

404
00:31:45,380 --> 00:31:47,650
He was going to execute me.

405
00:31:48,110 --> 00:31:49,970
He knew I was innocent.

406
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:52,220
He didn't hate me because of anything I did,

407
00:31:52,220 --> 00:31:54,530
he hated me because of what I am.

408
00:31:54,530 --> 00:31:57,470
A little monster sent to punish him.

409
00:31:59,590 --> 00:32:02,090
Did he... did he think...

410
00:32:02,100 --> 00:32:03,390
did he think I wanted to be born this way?

411
00:32:03,390 --> 00:32:05,830
- Did he think I chose it? - What do you want?!

412
00:32:12,220 --> 00:32:14,200
Daenerys will win this war.

413
00:32:16,140 --> 00:32:17,680
You're a military man.

414
00:32:17,880 --> 00:32:19,830
You must know there's no way around that.

415
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,290
Daenerys is not her father.

416
00:32:24,650 --> 00:32:26,490
She's even willing to suspend the hostilities

417
00:32:26,490 --> 00:32:29,000
if Cersei agrees to certain terms.

418
00:32:30,610 --> 00:32:31,960
If you want Cersei to bend the knee,

419
00:32:31,960 --> 00:32:32,900
you can ask her yourself.

420
00:32:32,900 --> 00:32:35,770
I don't. And Daenerys doesn't.

421
00:32:37,210 --> 00:32:38,590
Not right now, anyway.

422
00:32:40,920 --> 00:32:43,090
She has a more important request.

423
00:33:22,550 --> 00:33:24,460
I wasn't sure I'd find you.

424
00:33:32,050 --> 00:33:33,920
Thought you might still be rowing.

425
00:33:37,710 --> 00:33:40,460
I looked in shops, taverns, brothels.

426
00:33:41,130 --> 00:33:44,040
Should have known to come straight to the Street of Steel.

427
00:33:44,330 --> 00:33:46,750
Aren't you worried about the gold cloaks?

428
00:33:46,760 --> 00:33:48,230
Haven't been here in years.

429
00:33:48,420 --> 00:33:50,250
Why should they recognize me?

430
00:33:50,760 --> 00:33:52,490
Sometimes I hardly do.

431
00:33:54,770 --> 00:33:57,100
Nothing fucks you harder than time.

432
00:34:02,340 --> 00:34:04,030
Anybody give you any trouble?

433
00:34:04,170 --> 00:34:06,050
Here I am, arming Lannisters,

434
00:34:06,060 --> 00:34:08,160
and I never get a second look.

435
00:34:08,320 --> 00:34:09,550
But you were right.

436
00:34:09,550 --> 00:34:12,030
Safest place for me was right under the queen's nose.

437
00:34:12,030 --> 00:34:13,340
Don't be so sure.

438
00:34:13,340 --> 00:34:16,610
Safety is never a permanent state of affairs.

439
00:34:18,790 --> 00:34:20,370
Bad things are coming.

440
00:34:22,950 --> 00:34:25,920
You came to get me. You want me to come with you.

441
00:34:25,920 --> 00:34:27,660
- Well, the thing you need to understand is... - I'm ready.

442
00:34:27,660 --> 00:34:28,970
- You... - Let's go.

443
00:34:29,470 --> 00:34:31,240
You should know what you're heading into.

444
00:34:31,250 --> 00:34:32,990
What do you think I've been thinking about

445
00:34:32,990 --> 00:34:34,750
with every swing of the hammer?

446
00:34:35,030 --> 00:34:37,090
How happy I am making weapons

447
00:34:37,090 --> 00:34:39,040
for the family that killed my father?

448
00:34:39,900 --> 00:34:41,470
The family that tried to kill me?

449
00:34:43,560 --> 00:34:44,860
I've been getting ready.

450
00:34:45,970 --> 00:34:46,970
I never knew what for,

451
00:34:46,970 --> 00:34:49,460
but I've always known I'd know it when it comes.

452
00:34:51,490 --> 00:34:53,710
You might want to bring one of those swords.

453
00:34:54,530 --> 00:34:56,760
I don't know much about swinging swords.

454
00:34:57,740 --> 00:34:58,920
But this

455
00:35:00,730 --> 00:35:02,080
this I know.

456
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:13,280
Keep your father's name to yourself.

457
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:15,750
Situation's complicated enough already.

458
00:35:17,190 --> 00:35:18,850
Well, who should I say I am?

459
00:35:22,940 --> 00:35:24,840
I told you, Clovis, if we don't get out of here soon,

460
00:35:24,840 --> 00:35:26,530
- someone's going to... - You there!

461
00:35:28,880 --> 00:35:31,200
No weapons, friends. I promise.

462
00:35:32,850 --> 00:35:33,800
What can I do for you?

463
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:35,530
- Is that your boat? - It is.

464
00:35:36,530 --> 00:35:38,880
- The docks are that way. - That they are.

465
00:35:39,020 --> 00:35:40,470
I try to stay away from them

466
00:35:40,470 --> 00:35:42,850
to avoid good men such as yourselves.

467
00:35:45,520 --> 00:35:48,550
- Still five gold dragons? - Are you joking?

468
00:35:48,720 --> 00:35:50,960
You must be even older than you look.

469
00:35:50,960 --> 00:35:52,840
- 15. - 15?!

470
00:35:52,840 --> 00:35:54,050
Apiece.

471
00:36:02,600 --> 00:36:04,940
I can't say it was a pleasure doing business with you.

472
00:36:07,380 --> 00:36:08,670
What's in the boat?

473
00:36:13,870 --> 00:36:15,480
Not more gold.

474
00:36:15,560 --> 00:36:16,790
Wine?

475
00:36:16,790 --> 00:36:19,430
- I like wine. - Or hams.

476
00:36:21,010 --> 00:36:22,210
Come have a look.

477
00:36:30,620 --> 00:36:32,530
- Fermented crab. - What?

478
00:36:32,530 --> 00:36:34,230
Fermented crab.

479
00:36:34,230 --> 00:36:37,480
One bucket of this triples a brothel's earnings for the week.

480
00:36:37,480 --> 00:36:39,080
A man thinks he's done.

481
00:36:39,370 --> 00:36:41,710
He's ready to go back to his loving family.

482
00:36:41,710 --> 00:36:43,210
But before he gets his breeches up,

483
00:36:43,210 --> 00:36:47,150
his lady of the hour pops a tiny spoon of that into his mouth.

484
00:36:47,150 --> 00:36:49,940
Five minutes later, he's back in the race.

485
00:36:50,590 --> 00:36:53,350
Here, have a taste.

486
00:37:05,770 --> 00:37:07,660
I'd hurry to your favorite establishment,

487
00:37:07,660 --> 00:37:09,880
or you'll put a hole in that chainmail.

488
00:37:37,350 --> 00:37:39,190
Oi, dwarf!

489
00:37:40,830 --> 00:37:42,030
I really wouldn't try any more

490
00:37:42,030 --> 00:37:43,820
until you see how the first bite hits you.

491
00:37:43,830 --> 00:37:45,210
That dwarf...

492
00:37:45,880 --> 00:37:47,600
Where'd you get that scar?

493
00:37:47,710 --> 00:37:49,920
Fish hook. Some men you just can't teach.

494
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:53,540
We was looking for a dwarf with a scar like that a while back.

495
00:37:53,630 --> 00:37:55,700
Perhaps there's some arrangement?

496
00:37:57,740 --> 00:37:59,170
Arrangement?

497
00:37:59,940 --> 00:38:03,380
You gonna arrange to pay us more than Queen Cersei...

498
00:38:11,450 --> 00:38:12,780
This is Gendry.

499
00:38:13,360 --> 00:38:14,440
He'll do.

500
00:38:16,370 --> 00:38:17,610
Go, go, go.

501
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:21,790
I could give you something.

502
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:23,340
That won't be necessary.

503
00:38:32,130 --> 00:38:33,110
Ser Jaime.

504
00:38:36,980 --> 00:38:38,460
Why was Qyburn here?

505
00:38:39,890 --> 00:38:41,810
He's the Hand of the Queen. Why are you here?

506
00:38:46,880 --> 00:38:48,490
I met with Tyrion.

507
00:38:57,790 --> 00:38:59,290
What did our brother have to say?

508
00:39:02,470 --> 00:39:04,180
Daenerys wants to meet.

509
00:39:04,910 --> 00:39:06,560
To discuss her surrender?

510
00:39:07,720 --> 00:39:09,410
To discuss an armistice.

511
00:39:09,410 --> 00:39:12,260
She's just won a great victory. Why would she want a truce now?

512
00:39:12,260 --> 00:39:14,020
Because an army of dead men

513
00:39:14,020 --> 00:39:16,210
is marching on the Seven Kingdoms.

514
00:39:19,260 --> 00:39:21,210
Tyrion claims he'll have proof.

515
00:39:24,970 --> 00:39:27,090
- Are you going to punish him? - Tyrion?

516
00:39:27,090 --> 00:39:28,160
Bronn.

517
00:39:31,160 --> 00:39:32,530
He betrayed you.

518
00:39:33,750 --> 00:39:36,260
He set up a meeting without your knowledge or consent.

519
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:40,870
Do you think anything of importance

520
00:39:40,870 --> 00:39:43,160
happens in this city without me knowing?

521
00:39:44,640 --> 00:39:46,850
You let it happen. Why?

522
00:39:46,860 --> 00:39:49,210
I've come to believe that

523
00:39:49,470 --> 00:39:51,600
an accommodation with the Dragon Queen

524
00:39:52,200 --> 00:39:54,360
could be in our immediate interest.

525
00:39:54,920 --> 00:39:55,720
She has the numbers.

526
00:39:55,720 --> 00:39:57,780
If we want to beat her, we have to be clever.

527
00:39:58,040 --> 00:40:00,070
We have to fight her like Father would have.

528
00:40:03,790 --> 00:40:07,070
Dead men, dragons, and Dragon Queens...

529
00:40:08,970 --> 00:40:13,530
Whatever stands in our way, we will defeat it.

530
00:40:14,330 --> 00:40:16,410
For ourselves, for our house,

531
00:40:17,210 --> 00:40:18,280
for this.

532
00:40:31,240 --> 00:40:32,720
Who will you say is the father?

533
00:40:32,850 --> 00:40:33,760
You.

534
00:40:40,020 --> 00:40:41,320
People won't like that.

535
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:48,290
Do you remember what father used to say about people?

536
00:40:49,340 --> 00:40:53,010
The lion does not concern himself with the opinions of the sheep.

537
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:08,390
Never betray me again.

538
00:41:14,650 --> 00:41:15,900
We're leaving today.

539
00:41:16,220 --> 00:41:19,370
- The king's got a lot on his mind. - I understand.

540
00:41:19,370 --> 00:41:20,000
He doesn't need to be thinking

541
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:22,190
about harboring the bastard of a dead king.

542
00:41:22,190 --> 00:41:24,710
- You don't have to worry. - You're just Clovis,

543
00:41:24,770 --> 00:41:27,100
a smith who's come to pay his respects

544
00:41:27,100 --> 00:41:30,050
before he heads off to work at the Winterfell forges.

545
00:41:30,090 --> 00:41:31,070
Understood.

546
00:41:33,350 --> 00:41:34,890
Begging your pardon, Your Grace.

547
00:41:35,750 --> 00:41:37,100
You survived King's Landing.

548
00:41:37,100 --> 00:41:40,040
Yet again. Your Grace, this is Clo-

549
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:41,780
Name's Gendry, Your Grace.

550
00:41:42,520 --> 00:41:44,120
I'm Robert Baratheon's son.

551
00:41:44,160 --> 00:41:45,360
Bastard son.

552
00:41:48,250 --> 00:41:50,360
He was meant to keep that to himself.

553
00:41:50,370 --> 00:41:52,200
Our fathers trusted each other.

554
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:53,460
Why shouldn't we?

555
00:41:56,210 --> 00:41:58,550
I saw your father once at Winterfell.

556
00:41:58,890 --> 00:42:01,530
I met yours in my shop.

557
00:42:03,700 --> 00:42:06,460
- You're a lot leaner. - And you're a lot shorter.

558
00:42:16,100 --> 00:42:18,530
I grew up on stories about them.

559
00:42:19,800 --> 00:42:22,940
All I ever knew is that they fought together and won.

560
00:42:24,510 --> 00:42:27,350
Ser Davos told me where you're going, Your Grace, and why.

561
00:42:27,750 --> 00:42:28,840
Let me come with you.

562
00:42:29,100 --> 00:42:30,720
Don't be a fool. You're not a soldier.

563
00:42:30,720 --> 00:42:32,290
No, but I'm a fighter.

564
00:42:33,220 --> 00:42:35,570
And he won't be needing a smith with a sword like that.

565
00:42:38,430 --> 00:42:39,670
You know how to use one?

566
00:42:40,440 --> 00:42:41,810
Well, that's a problem.

567
00:42:42,240 --> 00:42:43,420
I prefer a hammer.

568
00:42:46,690 --> 00:42:48,080
He can handle himself.

569
00:42:50,410 --> 00:42:51,680
We could use the help.

570
00:42:52,280 --> 00:42:53,910
As my father used to say,

571
00:42:54,190 --> 00:42:56,090
"It's better to be a coward for a minute,

572
00:42:56,440 --> 00:42:58,280
than dead for the rest of your life."

573
00:42:59,410 --> 00:43:00,910
I owe you my life.

574
00:43:01,210 --> 00:43:02,300
Twice over.

575
00:43:03,060 --> 00:43:05,450
But if what you said is true about what's up there,

576
00:43:06,220 --> 00:43:08,010
I can't wait out this war.

577
00:43:12,440 --> 00:43:13,830
Yeah, nobody mind me.

578
00:43:14,270 --> 00:43:17,200
All I've ever done is live to a ripe old age.

579
00:43:18,160 --> 00:43:19,450
All right, come on.

580
00:43:29,660 --> 00:43:31,120
You may not believe it,

581
00:43:32,290 --> 00:43:33,650
but I've missed you, Mormont.

582
00:43:34,780 --> 00:43:36,840
Nobody glowers quite like you.

583
00:43:37,820 --> 00:43:39,070
Not even Grey Worm.

584
00:43:44,960 --> 00:43:46,850
This is the coin the slaver gave me

585
00:43:46,990 --> 00:43:49,720
when I suggested he free us and pay us, remember?

586
00:43:50,260 --> 00:43:53,080
It was supposed to last us the rest of our lives.

587
00:43:57,940 --> 00:43:58,920
Take it with you.

588
00:44:02,110 --> 00:44:03,280
But bring it back.

589
00:44:03,890 --> 00:44:05,080
Our queen needs you.

590
00:44:14,350 --> 00:44:16,550
We should be better at saying farewell by now.

591
00:44:18,550 --> 00:44:19,920
Your Grace, I...

592
00:44:37,190 --> 00:44:39,360
If I don't return, at least you won't have to deal

593
00:44:39,360 --> 00:44:41,200
with the King in the North anymore.

594
00:44:43,190 --> 00:44:44,440
I've grown used to him.

595
00:44:47,440 --> 00:44:50,220
I wish you good fortune in the wars to come, Your Grace.

596
00:44:58,780 --> 00:45:00,230
Heave.

597
00:45:23,910 --> 00:45:26,950
Do you know how many steps there are in the Citadel?

598
00:45:27,980 --> 00:45:28,980
No.

599
00:45:36,990 --> 00:45:40,220
Guess how many windows are in the Great Sept of Baelor.

600
00:45:42,300 --> 00:45:43,710
None anymore.

601
00:45:45,000 --> 00:45:46,230
That's true.

602
00:45:46,640 --> 00:45:50,720
This High Septon Maynard, he recorded everything.

603
00:45:50,720 --> 00:45:54,010
He even recorded his own bowel movements.

604
00:45:56,760 --> 00:46:00,120
What does "Annulment" Mean?

605
00:46:00,120 --> 00:46:03,800
It's when a man sets aside his lawful wife.

606
00:46:03,970 --> 00:46:05,750
Maynard says here that

607
00:46:05,750 --> 00:46:09,410
he issued an annulment for a Prince "Ragger"

608
00:46:09,410 --> 00:46:12,630
and remarried him to someone else at the same time

609
00:46:12,630 --> 00:46:15,220
in a secret ceremony in Dorne.

610
00:46:15,220 --> 00:46:17,000
Is that a common thing in the south or--?

611
00:46:17,000 --> 00:46:18,630
These maesters...

612
00:46:20,370 --> 00:46:23,900
they set me to the task of preserving that man's window counting

613
00:46:23,900 --> 00:46:26,600
and annulments and bowel movements for all eternity,

614
00:46:26,600 --> 00:46:27,840
while the secret to defeating the Night King's

615
00:46:27,840 --> 00:46:28,480
probably sitting on some

616
00:46:28,480 --> 00:46:30,780
dusty shelf somewhere, completely ignored.

617
00:46:31,100 --> 00:46:32,560
But that's all right, isn't it?

618
00:46:32,570 --> 00:46:34,370
We can all become slavering,

619
00:46:34,380 --> 00:46:36,600
murderous imbeciles in thrall to evil incarnate

620
00:46:36,600 --> 00:46:38,140
as long as we can have access to the full records

621
00:46:38,140 --> 00:46:42,150
of High Septon Maynard's 15,782 shits!

622
00:46:44,750 --> 00:46:46,140
Steps.

623
00:46:49,340 --> 00:46:51,880
That number was the steps.

624
00:48:13,370 --> 00:48:15,590
Are you sure you want to do this?

625
00:48:16,050 --> 00:48:18,450
You always wanted to be a maester.

626
00:48:20,150 --> 00:48:24,020
I'm tired of reading about the achievements of better men.

627
00:49:53,530 --> 00:49:55,110
I found it, my lord.

628
00:49:59,020 --> 00:50:00,630
It, uh, took some searching.

629
00:50:00,630 --> 00:50:02,740
Maester Luwin's archives are very thorough.

630
00:50:07,440 --> 00:50:09,660
You're sure this is the only copy in Winterfell?

631
00:50:09,950 --> 00:50:11,680
Uh, yes, my lord.

632
00:50:16,730 --> 00:50:19,060
Lady Stark thanks you for your service.

633
00:52:50,730 --> 00:52:54,700
Isn't it your job to talk him out of stupid fucking ideas like this?

634
00:52:54,700 --> 00:52:56,880
I've been failing at that job of late.

635
00:52:58,730 --> 00:53:00,550
How many queens are there now?

636
00:53:01,120 --> 00:53:02,140
Two.

637
00:53:02,510 --> 00:53:05,440
And you need to convince the one with the dragons

638
00:53:05,440 --> 00:53:07,320
or the one who fucks her brother?

639
00:53:09,060 --> 00:53:10,200
Both.

640
00:53:10,570 --> 00:53:12,070
How many men did you bring?

641
00:53:15,620 --> 00:53:16,690
Not enough.

642
00:53:17,420 --> 00:53:18,490
The big woman?

643
00:53:21,990 --> 00:53:24,770
We were hoping some of your men could help.

644
00:53:26,160 --> 00:53:27,380
I'll be staying behind.

645
00:53:27,380 --> 00:53:29,570
I'm a liability out there, as you well know.

646
00:53:30,550 --> 00:53:31,470
You are.

647
00:53:34,460 --> 00:53:37,770
You really want to go out there? Again?

648
00:53:43,850 --> 00:53:45,510
You're not the only ones.

649
00:53:49,500 --> 00:53:52,280
My scouts found them a mile south of the Wall.

650
00:53:52,740 --> 00:53:54,870
Said they were on their way here.

651
00:54:01,520 --> 00:54:02,700
You're the Hound.

652
00:54:04,960 --> 00:54:07,050
I saw you once at Winterfell.

653
00:54:12,610 --> 00:54:14,770
They want to go beyond the Wall, too.

654
00:54:14,770 --> 00:54:17,110
We don't want to go beyond the Wall, we have to.

655
00:54:17,990 --> 00:54:19,950
Our Lord told us that the Great War is coming--

656
00:54:19,950 --> 00:54:21,400
Don't trust him.

657
00:54:22,150 --> 00:54:23,580
Don't trust any of them.

658
00:54:29,910 --> 00:54:31,140
They're the Brotherhood.

659
00:54:31,920 --> 00:54:33,920
And the last thing their lord told them to do

660
00:54:33,920 --> 00:54:36,690
was sell me to a red witch to be murdered.

661
00:54:36,930 --> 00:54:38,090
Thoros?

662
00:54:43,140 --> 00:54:44,770
I hardly recognized you.

663
00:54:45,390 --> 00:54:47,340
Ser Jorah Mormont.

664
00:54:47,670 --> 00:54:50,330
They won't give me anything to drink down here.

665
00:54:50,700 --> 00:54:52,780
I haven't been feeling like myself.

666
00:54:53,400 --> 00:54:55,550
You're a fucking Mormont?

667
00:54:56,530 --> 00:54:58,520
Like the last Lord Commander?

668
00:54:59,570 --> 00:55:00,830
He was my father.

669
00:55:00,830 --> 00:55:03,850
He hunted us like animals.

670
00:55:03,890 --> 00:55:06,480
You returned the favor, as I recall.

671
00:55:08,780 --> 00:55:10,160
Here we all are

672
00:55:11,070 --> 00:55:12,660
at the edge of the world

673
00:55:12,830 --> 00:55:14,260
at the same moment,

674
00:55:14,310 --> 00:55:16,990
heading in the same direction for the same reason.

675
00:55:18,380 --> 00:55:20,720
Our reasons aren't your reasons.

676
00:55:20,720 --> 00:55:23,160
It doesn't matter what we think our reasons are.

677
00:55:25,320 --> 00:55:27,400
There's a greater purpose at work.

678
00:55:28,250 --> 00:55:29,810
And we serve it together,

679
00:55:30,450 --> 00:55:32,370
whether we know it or not.

680
00:55:33,100 --> 00:55:35,510
We may take the steps, but the Lord of Light--

681
00:55:35,510 --> 00:55:38,470
For fuck's sake, will you shut your hole?

682
00:55:38,800 --> 00:55:40,860
Are we coming with you or not?

683
00:55:41,790 --> 00:55:43,530
Don't you want to know what we're doing?

684
00:55:44,020 --> 00:55:47,690
Is it worse than sitting in a freezing cell, waiting to die?

685
00:55:48,250 --> 00:55:49,320
He's right.

686
00:55:50,900 --> 00:55:52,510
We're all on the same side.

687
00:55:55,260 --> 00:55:56,360
How can we be?

688
00:55:57,700 --> 00:55:59,150
We're all breathing.

